1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,669
"Healthy Seongsu Man."

2
00:00:02,670 --> 00:00:04,499
(Healthy Seongsu Man's New Challenge)

3
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:06,020
How am I going to organize everything?

4
00:00:06,328 --> 00:00:08,198
Let me fold the laundry first.

5
00:00:16,508 --> 00:00:18,367
(His dressing room is cluttered with clothes.)

6
00:00:18,368 --> 00:00:19,978
You have a lot of clothes.

7
00:00:20,378 --> 00:00:21,838
I just can't seem to organize them.

8
00:00:22,108 --> 00:00:23,948
I ought to pay you a visit.

9
00:00:26,578 --> 00:00:28,338
You really love the hospital shade of green.

10
00:00:28,448 --> 00:00:29,518
It's deep green.

11
00:00:31,388 --> 00:00:34,388
(They seem to be organized and chaotic at the same time.)

12
00:00:35,318 --> 00:00:36,758
Once my clothes started to pile up,

13
00:00:36,988 --> 00:00:38,958
I gradually gave up on keeping them tidy.

14
00:00:39,598 --> 00:00:42,927
They began to turn into a mess and I neglected the mess.

15
00:00:42,928 --> 00:00:46,768
So my dressing room is the least organized room now.

16
00:00:47,038 --> 00:00:50,268
I just throw everything I don't want to see in that room.

17
00:00:50,468 --> 00:00:51,838
- Of course. - Everyone does that.

18
00:00:52,168 --> 00:00:54,077
Well, it's like a pancreas.

19
00:00:54,078 --> 00:00:55,078
- What? - A pancreas?

20
00:00:55,079 --> 00:00:56,439
Things get filtered through there.

21
00:00:57,008 --> 00:00:58,177
You studied a lot about medicine...

22
00:00:58,178 --> 00:00:59,658
since you live in Severance Hospital.

23
00:00:59,848 --> 00:01:01,847
I found out about the function of pancreas...

24
00:01:01,848 --> 00:01:03,118
- just now. - Same here.

25
00:01:03,348 --> 00:01:06,288
(The color of knowledge in 2026, deep green)

26
00:01:08,018 --> 00:01:09,358
Gosh, what do I do?

27
00:01:10,288 --> 00:01:11,787
- You should bring everything down. - Seriously?

28
00:01:11,788 --> 00:01:14,397
- You must do it without any regret. - Right.

29
00:01:14,398 --> 00:01:15,997
Getting started is always tough.

30
00:01:15,998 --> 00:01:17,767
Right. Once you get started, it goes smoothly.

31
00:01:17,768 --> 00:01:18,768
Right.

32
00:01:19,098 --> 00:01:20,268
That too...

33
00:01:21,438 --> 00:01:22,667
I don't know where to begin.

34
00:01:22,668 --> 00:01:23,708
(Grabbing)

35
00:01:24,268 --> 00:01:25,338
This...

36
00:01:26,208 --> 00:01:27,738
(Glancing up)

37
00:01:28,378 --> 00:01:29,448
Sweater.

38
00:01:31,308 --> 00:01:32,448
Is it a short sleeve shirt?

39
00:01:34,018 --> 00:01:36,048
Short sleeve shirt. Hoodie.

40
00:01:37,288 --> 00:01:38,587
It will take forever at that rate.

41
00:01:38,588 --> 00:01:39,788
Long sleeve shirt.

42
00:01:40,258 --> 00:01:41,288
Hoodie.

43
00:01:42,958 --> 00:01:46,628
I wanted to get rid of my old clothes.

44
00:01:46,898 --> 00:01:48,057
That crossed my mind.

45
00:01:48,058 --> 00:01:49,767
I didn't wear some of those clothes for a year...

46
00:01:49,768 --> 00:01:51,528
which means I won't wear them.

47
00:01:51,628 --> 00:01:53,167
So I decided to follow my gut and make quick decisions...

48
00:01:53,168 --> 00:01:54,697
while going through my clothes.

49
00:01:54,698 --> 00:01:56,458
Once I saw fit to throw out certain clothes,

50
00:01:56,568 --> 00:01:59,608
I decided to sort them out without hesitation.

51
00:02:00,608 --> 00:02:01,807
(He starts sorting out clothes that need to be thrown out.)

52
00:02:01,808 --> 00:02:03,208
Gosh, you'll pick and choose?

53
00:02:03,348 --> 00:02:05,747
I was going to throw out some old clothes without hesitation.

54
00:02:05,748 --> 00:02:06,748
(Let me see.)

55
00:02:06,918 --> 00:02:08,118
I wore this for a long time.

56
00:02:08,948 --> 00:02:10,308
Since I wore it for a long time...

57
00:02:12,818 --> 00:02:13,888
Bye.

58
00:02:15,018 --> 00:02:16,188
(Tossing)

59
00:02:17,388 --> 00:02:18,458
These too.

60
00:02:20,498 --> 00:02:21,618
I'll throw out most of them.

61
00:02:22,198 --> 00:02:24,297
This process will make you more thoughtful when buying clothes.

62
00:02:24,298 --> 00:02:25,568
- Right. - Yes.

63
00:02:26,468 --> 00:02:27,668
Green pants.

64
00:02:29,808 --> 00:02:31,268
I might wear them at some point.

65
00:02:33,078 --> 00:02:35,178
I can't throw out deep green pants. I'll keep them.

66
00:02:35,438 --> 00:02:37,778
(Deep green shorts survive.)

67
00:02:41,318 --> 00:02:42,448
They are comfortable too.

68
00:02:42,618 --> 00:02:45,147
Here's the sentence that tempts you the most when throwing out clothes.

69
00:02:45,148 --> 00:02:46,188
"I'll wear them at home."

70
00:02:46,318 --> 00:02:48,087
- "I'll wear them as pajamas." - Yes. "I'll wear them as pajamas."

71
00:02:48,088 --> 00:02:49,157
That's the most dangerous one.

72
00:02:49,158 --> 00:02:50,288
(Thinking)

73
00:02:50,658 --> 00:02:52,058
I'll probably wear them as pajamas.

74
00:02:52,158 --> 00:02:53,258
(Embarrassed)

75
00:02:54,528 --> 00:02:55,598
Pants.

76
00:02:56,298 --> 00:02:58,228
(Unfolding)

77
00:02:59,498 --> 00:03:00,667
Aren't they all the same pants?

78
00:03:00,668 --> 00:03:01,838
Aren't they all pajamas?

79
00:03:02,038 --> 00:03:03,568
(They do look similar.)

80
00:03:03,838 --> 00:03:05,508
I don't want any of your clothes.

81
00:03:06,478 --> 00:03:07,718
I usually go crazy for clothes.

82
00:03:09,208 --> 00:03:11,848
You should get rid of everything since you won't wear any of them.

83
00:03:12,778 --> 00:03:15,517
Then what am I going to wear if I do that?

84
00:03:15,518 --> 00:03:17,217
I usually think, "Why is he throwing them out?"

85
00:03:17,218 --> 00:03:18,218
"What a waste."

86
00:03:18,219 --> 00:03:19,787
- But nothing really stands out. - You can stay calm, right?

87
00:03:19,788 --> 00:03:21,668
- Right. Looking at his clothes... - Same here.

88
00:03:21,718 --> 00:03:23,327
He and I basically have the same clothes.

89
00:03:23,328 --> 00:03:24,888
Then you sorted out your clothes too?

90
00:03:25,088 --> 00:03:26,557
Clothes even I won't wear...

91
00:03:26,558 --> 00:03:28,027
- must be thrown out. - Right.

92
00:03:28,028 --> 00:03:30,028
I see a lot of such clothes in his room.

93
00:03:31,968 --> 00:03:34,968
I took a look at his room. He's in a pretty tough situation.

94
00:03:38,038 --> 00:03:39,068
Short sleeve shirts.

95
00:03:39,168 --> 00:03:40,807
You need to do a good job with short sleeve shirts.

96
00:03:40,808 --> 00:03:41,878
Start from number one.

97
00:03:43,748 --> 00:03:45,478
Go to number three and grab it.

98
00:03:46,878 --> 00:03:47,948
Turn it.

99
00:03:49,548 --> 00:03:50,618
After turning it...

100
00:03:50,748 --> 00:03:52,047
- What? - You see that in clothing stores.

101
00:03:52,048 --> 00:03:53,418
- There. - I see.

102
00:03:54,388 --> 00:03:55,588
I'll fold this one more time.

103
00:03:57,658 --> 00:03:58,987
That's neat.

104
00:03:58,988 --> 00:04:00,057
How did you do that?

105
00:04:00,058 --> 00:04:02,058
- That's the retail-style fold. - How interesting.

106
00:04:02,128 --> 00:04:04,674
That's the first thing you learn while working at clothing stores.

107
00:04:04,698 --> 00:04:06,298
(Leaning forward)

108
00:04:06,768 --> 00:04:09,138
- I bet there are 1,000 of them. - Right.

109
00:04:09,708 --> 00:04:11,367
I used to work briefly in a clothing store...

110
00:04:11,368 --> 00:04:12,808
- Really? - a long time ago.

111
00:04:13,008 --> 00:04:15,177
I have my own method of folding clothes. It only takes a second.

112
00:04:15,178 --> 00:04:16,307
- Do it. - How?

113
00:04:16,308 --> 00:04:17,947
- I don't buy that. One second? - You grab it.

114
00:04:17,948 --> 00:04:19,478
- And then? - Then you do this.

115
00:04:19,878 --> 00:04:20,978
Then you do this.

116
00:04:21,678 --> 00:04:22,717
- What? - How...

117
00:04:22,718 --> 00:04:24,118
You're just folding it in half.

118
00:04:26,488 --> 00:04:27,817
You're just folding it in half.

119
00:04:27,818 --> 00:04:29,428
(Puzzled)

120
00:04:29,828 --> 00:04:31,028
Let's do it with a T-shirt.

121
00:04:31,488 --> 00:04:33,368
- I'm so curious. I must see it. - I'm curious.

122
00:04:33,398 --> 00:04:34,498
I see. That?

123
00:04:35,058 --> 00:04:36,127
Gosh, that's...

124
00:04:36,128 --> 00:04:38,127
- Wait. I... - You're stripping down Wilson.

125
00:04:38,128 --> 00:04:40,668
- Will it work with that? - Let's learn it.

126
00:04:40,938 --> 00:04:41,967
- Will it work with a hoodie? - So...

127
00:04:41,968 --> 00:04:43,967
- One-second fold. - Gosh, it will take a second.

128
00:04:43,968 --> 00:04:45,144
- Because it's a hoodie? - Let's watch.

129
00:04:45,168 --> 00:04:46,808
(All eyes are on him.)

130
00:04:46,978 --> 00:04:49,098
(Those of you who had a tough time folding clothes, )

131
00:04:49,238 --> 00:04:53,078
(check out my 1-second secret method.)

132
00:04:54,418 --> 00:04:55,617
All right. Go ahead.

133
00:04:55,618 --> 00:04:57,418
- Are you done shopping? - Yes.

134
00:04:58,348 --> 00:04:59,557
All right. Go ahead.

135
00:04:59,558 --> 00:05:01,217
- Are you done shopping? - Yes.

136
00:05:01,218 --> 00:05:02,258
Like that.

137
00:05:05,088 --> 00:05:07,328
- What is that? - Hey. What is this?

138
00:05:07,858 --> 00:05:09,127
(Looking like messy laundry)

139
00:05:09,128 --> 00:05:11,427
- What is that? - That's really iffy.

140
00:05:11,428 --> 00:05:12,467
It's all crumpled up.

141
00:05:12,468 --> 00:05:15,367
Right. With my method, it's not as neat as it should be.

142
00:05:15,368 --> 00:05:16,888
- Is it because it's a hoodie? - So...

143
00:05:16,938 --> 00:05:18,838
there are just so many clothes to organize.

144
00:05:19,168 --> 00:05:20,278
(Trying to understand him)

145
00:05:20,708 --> 00:05:22,654
(His 1-second secret method is to fold clothes half-heartedly.)

146
00:05:22,678 --> 00:05:24,578
(Try my method. It's easy.)

147
00:05:24,778 --> 00:05:26,817
I'll put them back.

148
00:05:26,818 --> 00:05:27,978
(Putting away folded clothes)

149
00:05:29,518 --> 00:05:31,817
- That looks neat now. - You created more space now.

150
00:05:31,818 --> 00:05:33,988
- Yes. You must've thrown out half. - That's good.

151
00:05:34,658 --> 00:05:35,758
Great.

152
00:05:36,628 --> 00:05:37,657
That's good.

153
00:05:37,658 --> 00:05:38,957
(This time, he goes through his jackets.)

154
00:05:38,958 --> 00:05:40,058
This is good.

155
00:05:40,358 --> 00:05:42,728
(What's this jacket?)

156
00:05:43,798 --> 00:05:45,268
I rarely wear coats.

157
00:05:46,338 --> 00:05:47,778
You can film a period piece with it.

158
00:05:50,968 --> 00:05:52,068
I doubt I'll wear it.

159
00:05:53,708 --> 00:05:56,908
- A suit. - I hardly ever wear coats.

160
00:05:57,048 --> 00:05:58,947
- That one looks good. - This one looks nice.

161
00:05:58,948 --> 00:06:00,747
- It's nice. It looks good on you. - Really?

162
00:06:00,748 --> 00:06:02,247
- You should keep it. - But it's slightly big on you.

163
00:06:02,248 --> 00:06:03,418
I should throw it out too.

164
00:06:03,718 --> 00:06:04,718
I'll let it go.

165
00:06:04,719 --> 00:06:06,358
- No. Not that one. - What a pity.

166
00:06:06,718 --> 00:06:08,317
- I don't have an eye for this. - That one looked nice.

167
00:06:08,318 --> 00:06:09,318
You really don't.

168
00:06:10,288 --> 00:06:11,987
What if you only threw out good ones?

169
00:06:11,988 --> 00:06:13,728
(Oh, no)

170
00:06:14,658 --> 00:06:17,368
The most important point is that I must exclude my emotions.

171
00:06:18,028 --> 00:06:20,398
"My ex-girlfriend gave it to me as a birthday present."

172
00:06:20,698 --> 00:06:23,298
"My mom gave it to me as a present at my high school graduation."

173
00:06:23,608 --> 00:06:25,328
Then I won't be able to throw out anything.

174
00:06:25,808 --> 00:06:28,208
But I must throw them out for my mom to buy me more clothes.

175
00:06:29,608 --> 00:06:31,948
I must throw them out, so I can get a new girlfriend.

176
00:06:32,378 --> 00:06:33,477
That's the logic.

177
00:06:33,478 --> 00:06:35,447
(Looking for a girlfriend)

178
00:06:35,448 --> 00:06:36,748
Are you challenging me?

179
00:06:38,318 --> 00:06:39,894
The worst son this country has ever seen.

180
00:06:39,918 --> 00:06:41,394
Why throw out a present from your mom?

181
00:06:41,418 --> 00:06:42,788
That way, she'll buy him more.

182
00:06:43,958 --> 00:06:45,528
I think this will be a good match.

183
00:06:46,398 --> 00:06:47,627
You're catching up fast.

184
00:06:47,628 --> 00:06:48,798
So his mom can buy him more.

185
00:06:49,598 --> 00:06:51,868
I'm done picking out clothes to throw out. After this...

186
00:06:51,968 --> 00:06:53,128
I threw out a lot of clothes.

187
00:06:53,298 --> 00:06:55,598
(A bag full of clothes)

188
00:06:57,708 --> 00:07:00,678
(Gosh, I'm finally done.)

189
00:07:02,308 --> 00:07:04,747
(Before and after the cleaning session)

190
00:07:04,748 --> 00:07:06,578
- What has changed? - Wait. That's...

191
00:07:07,548 --> 00:07:09,987
- His shelves look a bit empty now. - Righit.

192
00:07:09,988 --> 00:07:11,147
He's gotten more space now.

193
00:07:11,148 --> 00:07:12,788
(Looking clean)

194
00:07:14,258 --> 00:07:15,388
Let me weigh this.

195
00:07:17,258 --> 00:07:18,528
(Tossing)

196
00:07:19,258 --> 00:07:20,958
(Stepping on it)

197
00:07:22,028 --> 00:07:23,168
It's 64.5kg.

198
00:07:23,968 --> 00:07:25,068
You're skinny.

199
00:07:26,968 --> 00:07:29,968
(He steps on the scale again with the bag.)

200
00:07:30,868 --> 00:07:32,008
It weighs 15kg.

201
00:07:32,608 --> 00:07:34,278
- Why are you weighing it? - It's 15kg.

202
00:07:34,808 --> 00:07:35,877
Can you accumulate points?

203
00:07:35,878 --> 00:07:37,048
(The 1st bag weighs 15kg.)

204
00:07:38,178 --> 00:07:39,277
It's 10kg.

205
00:07:39,278 --> 00:07:40,977
(The 2nd bag weighs 10kg.)

206
00:07:40,978 --> 00:07:42,077
It's 5kg.

207
00:07:42,078 --> 00:07:43,588
(The 3rd bag weighs 5kg.)

208
00:07:43,888 --> 00:07:46,518
That's 30kg in total.

209
00:07:47,388 --> 00:07:48,417
My gosh.

210
00:07:48,418 --> 00:07:50,858
So it's 30kg. I can do this.

211
00:07:52,058 --> 00:07:54,997
Okay. Let's go then.

212
00:07:54,998 --> 00:07:57,198
(Sounding determined)

213
00:07:59,468 --> 00:08:01,697
(He grabs the bags...)

214
00:08:01,698 --> 00:08:05,808
(and goes out briskly.)

215
00:08:12,348 --> 00:08:13,777
You're carrying 30kg?

216
00:08:13,778 --> 00:08:15,298
- It must hurt his shoulders. - Right.

217
00:08:15,378 --> 00:08:16,717
Why didn't you take your car? Why walk?

218
00:08:16,718 --> 00:08:18,518
(Ju Seung is heading somewhere on foot.)

219
00:08:18,918 --> 00:08:21,157
After watching the episode, the Grand Rainbow Bazaar,

220
00:08:21,158 --> 00:08:24,487
- I also wanted to donate. - That's good.

221
00:08:24,488 --> 00:08:25,857
- I was motivated to donate too. - That's great.

222
00:08:25,858 --> 00:08:29,058
I'm heading to a charity shop for secondhand items.

223
00:08:29,668 --> 00:08:30,798
That's good.

224
00:08:30,968 --> 00:08:33,968
The shop isn't that far away.

225
00:08:34,098 --> 00:08:36,337
So I wanted to walk there.

226
00:08:36,338 --> 00:08:39,368
On my way there, I wanted to look around my neighborhood again.

227
00:08:39,508 --> 00:08:40,677
There are some things you see...

228
00:08:40,678 --> 00:08:41,837
- when you take your time. - Right.

229
00:08:41,838 --> 00:08:43,048
I decided to walk there...

230
00:08:43,378 --> 00:08:45,247
because it'd be a nice chance to look around too.

231
00:08:45,248 --> 00:08:47,448
So I don't need to throw them out in the clothing box.

232
00:08:47,618 --> 00:08:49,848
I didn't bring clothes I was going to throw out.

233
00:08:50,088 --> 00:08:51,687
- I took clothes in good condition. - Right.

234
00:08:51,688 --> 00:08:52,818
- I see. - On purpose?

235
00:08:55,518 --> 00:08:59,128
(He walks while looking around the neighborhood.)

236
00:08:59,998 --> 00:09:01,558
My gosh, 30kg...

237
00:09:02,598 --> 00:09:03,628
is...

238
00:09:05,128 --> 00:09:06,268
heavier than I thought.

239
00:09:06,468 --> 00:09:09,497
- That's really heavy. - Right, it's so heavy.

240
00:09:09,498 --> 00:09:10,968
That's as heavy as full combat gear.

241
00:09:12,808 --> 00:09:13,808
(Exhaling)

242
00:09:14,178 --> 00:09:15,638
This is all part of my training.

243
00:09:18,278 --> 00:09:22,378
(He's been through a good number of intensive training.)

244
00:09:24,088 --> 00:09:25,817
(Today is just one of those training days.)

245
00:09:25,818 --> 00:09:27,218
He's Martial Artist Ju Seung.

246
00:09:27,688 --> 00:09:29,357
- It's a nice workout too. - Great.

247
00:09:29,358 --> 00:09:30,528
(This is a piece of cake.)

248
00:09:31,428 --> 00:09:35,798
(Exhaling)

249
00:09:37,468 --> 00:09:38,598
All right.

250
00:09:38,868 --> 00:09:41,337
The straps were digging into my shoulders quite painfully.

251
00:09:41,338 --> 00:09:42,574
- I bet. - You know what I mean, right?

252
00:09:42,598 --> 00:09:44,184
- The straps were digging into them. - It hurts.

253
00:09:44,208 --> 00:09:45,308
That was really painful.

254
00:09:47,708 --> 00:09:49,188
Gosh, that must've been really tough.

255
00:09:50,248 --> 00:09:51,347
It must be tough.

256
00:09:51,348 --> 00:09:53,248
(Staggering)

257
00:09:55,148 --> 00:09:58,647
(The more he walks, )

258
00:09:58,648 --> 00:10:00,588
(the heavier his steps feel.)

259
00:10:00,688 --> 00:10:03,627
- You should've taken a local bus. - It would've been so heavy.

260
00:10:03,628 --> 00:10:04,628
(Feeling sorry for him)

261
00:10:07,158 --> 00:10:09,998
(Slow)

262
00:10:10,128 --> 00:10:12,898
(Pausing)

263
00:10:16,468 --> 00:10:17,668
- What's that? - What is it?

264
00:10:19,978 --> 00:10:21,507
- It was someone's underwear. - What?

265
00:10:21,508 --> 00:10:22,608
(Abandoned on the street)

266
