2085
01:21:47,997 --> 01:21:49,127
Natto...

2086
01:21:49,597 --> 01:21:54,336
Natto cream cheese with pollack roe and perilla leaves...

2087
01:21:54,337 --> 01:21:55,897
over rice.

2088
01:21:56,807 --> 01:21:57,907
It doesn't look good.

2089
01:21:59,777 --> 01:22:01,477
It is good.

2090
01:22:02,077 --> 01:22:03,707
I don't like natto.

2091
01:22:06,147 --> 01:22:07,217
Ta-da.

2092
01:22:08,217 --> 01:22:09,947
It's braised kimchi.

2093
01:22:11,017 --> 01:22:13,457
That looks really good. I want to have rice with it.

2094
01:22:16,187 --> 01:22:17,886
They look like friends.

2095
01:22:17,887 --> 01:22:18,957
- I know. - Yes.

2096
01:22:19,087 --> 01:22:20,557
Try speaking in Korean.

2097
01:22:22,357 --> 01:22:24,297
Do you know how to say, "I want to eat it?"

2098
01:22:25,327 --> 01:22:27,167
I missed you.

2099
01:22:28,367 --> 01:22:29,637
She said something hard.

2100
01:22:30,367 --> 01:22:31,467
That's correct.

2101
01:22:31,867 --> 01:22:33,137
I want to eat it.

2102
01:22:33,777 --> 01:22:35,176
- I want to eat it! - Yes.

2103
01:22:35,177 --> 01:22:36,177
Her pronunciation is good.

2104
01:22:36,178 --> 01:22:38,707
What about "Thank you for the food?"

2105
01:22:39,817 --> 01:22:40,976
Thank you for the food.

2106
01:22:40,977 --> 01:22:43,417
(Thank you for the food.)

2107
01:22:45,017 --> 01:22:46,857
I practiced saying it really hard last time.

2108
01:22:47,887 --> 01:22:51,257
(She studies Korean with her mom.)

2109
01:22:54,257 --> 01:22:55,927
- That's your dad? - That's my dad!

2110
01:22:57,727 --> 01:22:59,497
Dad!

2111
01:23:00,967 --> 01:23:02,567
You worked hard today.

2112
01:23:03,167 --> 01:23:05,737
I called my parents.

2113
01:23:06,167 --> 01:23:08,407
I live in Korea,

2114
01:23:08,777 --> 01:23:11,207
my mom lives in Osaka,

2115
01:23:11,407 --> 01:23:14,817
and because of his work,

2116
01:23:15,017 --> 01:23:17,587
my dad lives in Hiroshima.

2117
01:23:17,687 --> 01:23:20,387
As we all live separately,

2118
01:23:21,057 --> 01:23:22,557
we're all lonely.

2119
01:23:22,787 --> 01:23:25,686
So we thought we should video call each other.

2120
01:23:25,687 --> 01:23:26,956
We video call each other often.

2121
01:23:26,957 --> 01:23:28,657
We do it almost every day these days.

2122
01:23:29,557 --> 01:23:31,027
You guys must miss each other a lot.

2123
01:23:31,827 --> 01:23:33,167
I snuck out.

2124
01:23:35,897 --> 01:23:37,137
I was having a team dinner.

2125
01:23:37,507 --> 01:23:38,707
You're going through a lot.

2126
01:23:39,037 --> 01:23:42,077
Do you know how to say that in Korean?

2127
01:23:42,877 --> 01:23:43,877
"It's all right."

2128
01:23:46,007 --> 01:23:48,123
- What do you mean it's all right? - "It's all right."

2129
01:23:48,147 --> 01:23:49,277
What's all right?

2130
01:23:50,187 --> 01:23:51,947
Is it "Thank you?"

2131
01:23:53,217 --> 01:23:54,287
"Thank you."

2132
01:23:55,687 --> 01:23:59,126
I got to learn about Korean culture...

2133
01:23:59,127 --> 01:24:00,896
through my mom and dad.

2134
01:24:00,897 --> 01:24:03,026
- No wonder. - So my mom would watch...

2135
01:24:03,027 --> 01:24:06,496
Korean period dramas or old dramas,

2136
01:24:06,497 --> 01:24:09,537
and I got to listen and learn Korean through them.

2137
01:24:09,837 --> 01:24:11,437
Your mom loves Korean dramas too, right?

2138
01:24:11,567 --> 01:24:13,066
It's called Jang...

2139
01:24:13,067 --> 01:24:15,013
- Oh, "Jewel in the Palace?" - Yes, "Jewel in the Palace!"

2140
01:24:15,037 --> 01:24:16,037
- "Jewel in the Palace." - Yes.

2141
01:24:16,038 --> 01:24:17,046
- Oh, "Jewel in the Palace?" - That's right.

2142
01:24:17,047 --> 01:24:18,577
I see, "Jewel in the Palace."

2143
01:24:18,677 --> 01:24:20,947
My father is a fan of TVXQ.

2144
01:24:21,147 --> 01:24:22,246
- Your father? - Yes.

2145
01:24:22,247 --> 01:24:23,347
- Really? - Really?

2146
01:24:23,747 --> 01:24:25,786
He's a fan of Shim Chang Min.

2147
01:24:25,787 --> 01:24:26,957
- Really? - Gosh.

2148
01:24:28,457 --> 01:24:32,427
You watched "Itaewon Class" a lot.

2149
01:24:35,097 --> 01:24:37,167
You could speak Korean a little back then.

2150
01:24:38,267 --> 01:24:41,336
He wanted to do the Park Sae Ro Yi hair,

2151
01:24:41,337 --> 01:24:42,767
